## Lessons Learned

- A silent black screen and an explicit "no bootable device" error are different failure modes that point to different layers of the stack (firmware/EFI initialization vs. boot device detection) — learning to distinguish them narrowed troubleshooting significantly.
- When two independently sourced files produce identical failures, suspect configuration over media. It's tempting to keep blaming the download, but ruling out the file early would have saved real time here.
- Comparing against a known-working baseline (the existing Win10/Ubuntu VMs) is more efficient than testing settings in isolation — the next step in this investigation is a direct line-by-line config diff against that baseline rather than continuing to guess at individual settings.
- Not every IT problem resolves on the expected timeline. Documenting an in-progress, unresolved issue with a clear methodology is itself a valid and realistic portfolio artifact.
